## Preflight for OpenSpec work

When creating or implementing an OpenSpec change, check whether the change introduces a
[formal trigger](docs/ARCHITECTURE_REASSESSMENT.md#formal-triggers), especially:

- ownership transfer for mutable state;
- state transition changes;
- new top-level abstractions, Managers, or parallel authorities;
- behavior that conflicts with archived specs or architecture docs.

If no formal trigger fired, use lightweight preflight: short inline owner/change/test summary
before implementation.

If a formal trigger fired, complete a full preflight before firmware edits:

- use `docs/Templates/PREFLIGHT.md`;
- include ownership-transfer fields when mutable ownership moves;
- include `docs/Templates/DECISION_REVIEW.md` or equivalent findings;
- create a repo artifact such as `openspec/changes/<name>/PREFLIGHT.md` when the OpenSpec
  itself carries the design/implementation handoff;
- add explicit `tasks.md` items for preflight, decision log entry, compatibility removal trigger,
  and validation gates.

## Terminology delta

A change that coins a term, reuses one with a new meaning, or deprecates one carries a `## Terminology` delta in
`openspec/changes/<name>/design.md`:

| Column | Meaning |
|--------|---------|
| Term | The word or identifier |
| Meaning | One line, in the owning layer's terms |
| Reuse or new | An existing governed term, or a new top-level domain noun (needs user approval and a `DEC-###`) |
| Status | `proposed` / `adopted` / `deprecated` |

Until the term is registered in [`docs/Authority/NAMING.md`](docs/Authority/NAMING.md) it is **provisional**: usable
inside that change, but not in shared docs, other plans or new code names. Precedence is claim-scoped — NAMING decides
names and meanings, OpenSpec decides behavior — see
[NAMING.md](docs/Authority/NAMING.md) § Scope of this authority.

| Command | Duty |
|---------|------|
| `/opsx:propose` | Add the delta when terms change; get approval first for a new top-level domain noun |
| `/opsx:apply` | Use adopted terms, or this change's provisional terms only — do not spread a provisional term into other docs |
| `/opsx:archive` | Promote the delta into `docs/Authority/NAMING.md` (with the `DEC-###`) or drop it explicitly, exactly as delta specs are promoted into `openspec/specs/` |

